<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The app's own mark, adapted for a quick settings tile.

     NOT ic_gloaming, which is a bare crescent: on the shade that sat two tiles
     from the system's own Do Not Disturb, also a crescent, and the two read as
     twins. The arc is what makes this one ours at a glance.

     GEOMETRY IS ic_launcher_foreground's, number for number - the bite of 18.48
     offset across the disc, the 0.86 on the crescent's own group, the arc at
     r=30.60 with a 4.0 stroke and round caps. The first version of this file
     copied ic_launcher_monochrome instead, which was carrying the OLD bite of
     19.74 and a 3.0 arc, so the tile drew a crescent 0.499 R thick where the
     icon draws one 0.776 R thick. It was reported as not looking like the app
     icon, and it did not. If those numbers move in the foreground they move
     here, and in ic_launcher_monochrome, in the same commit.

     WHAT IS DIFFERENT, and only this:

     Scale. The launcher keeps only the central 72dp of its 108dp canvas and
     scales up; a tile shows the whole box. So the launcher's balance group
     (0.92 with translateY 2.51) is replaced rather than kept - at 1.53 the
     artwork's outer extent, the arc's 30.60 plus half its 4.0 stroke, reaches
     r=49.9 of 54 and the mark spans about 22 of the 24dp box.

     That is essentially the ceiling. 32.6 x S must stay inside 54, so S cannot
     pass 1.656 without the arc clipping at the viewport edge, and the optical
     drop below spends some of what is left. There is no meaningful size left to
     find here - a mark that still reads small wants a heavier stroke, not a
     bigger box.

     The drop. translateY 4.17 is the launcher's 2.51 carried across the change
     of scale (2.51 x 1.53 / 0.92). It is not decoration: the arc's 113 degree
     gap is at the BOTTOM, so the ink sits above the centre of its own bounding
     box, and centring the box leaves the mark visibly high. The foreground's
     comment works this out at length; the same correction applies here for the
     same reason, scaled. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp" android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108" android:viewportHeight="108"
    android:tint="?android:attr/colorControlNormal">
    <group android:pivotX="54" android:pivotY="54"
           android:scaleX="1.53" android:scaleY="1.53"
           android:translateY="4.17">
        <group android:rotation="-32" android:pivotX="54" android:pivotY="54"
            android:scaleX="0.86" android:scaleY="0.86">
            <clip-path android:pathData="M33.00,54.00 a21.00,21.00 0 1,0 42.00,0 a21.00,21.00 0 1,0 -42.00,0 Z" />
            <path android:fillType="evenOdd" android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
                android:pathData="M33.00,54.00 a21.00,21.00 0 1,0 42.00,0 a21.00,21.00 0 1,0 -42.00,0 Z M46.43,45.59 a18.48,18.48 0 1,0 36.96,0 a18.48,18.48 0 1,0 -36.96,0 Z" />
        </group>
        <group android:rotation="90.95" android:pivotX="54" android:pivotY="54">
            <path
                android:pathData="M70.82,79.56 A30.60,30.60 0 0 1 30.95,74.12 A30.60,30.60 0 0 1 30.95,33.88 A30.60,30.60 0 0 1 70.82,28.44"
                android:strokeWidth="4.0" android:strokeLineCap="round"
                android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF" android:fillColor="#00000000" />
        </group>
    </group>
</vector>
